From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Mark the assertion-only locals of row_group.cpp as used

row_group.cpp declares locals that only D_ASSERT() reads (row_group),
so in a release build, where D_ASSERT() expands to nothing, they are unused
and -Wunused-variable or -Wunused-but-set-variable says so. Each is cast
to void after its declaration, which changes no behavior.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.

---
diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/storage/table/row_group.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/storage/table/row_group.cpp
--- a/src/duckdb/src/storage/table/row_group.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/storage/table/row_group.cpp
@@ -1434,6 +1434,7 @@ vector<RowGroupWriteData> RowGroup::WriteToDisk(RowGroupWriteInfo &info,
 
 	idx_t column_count = row_groups[0].get().GetColumnCount();
 	for (auto &row_group : row_groups) {
+		(void)row_group;
 		D_ASSERT(column_count == row_group.get().GetColumnCount());
 		RowGroupWriteData write_data;
 		write_data.states.reserve(column_count);
